{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall bring her into your house.</b> That is, he may not press himself upon her in war to lie with her more than a first act of intercourse, and the Torah prohibited only a second act of intercourse. And I say: not a second act and not a first act, but only after all these actions. And some explain: he may not press himself upon her in war — that he may not remove the garments she is wearing in war, and thus the verse implies that follows it: והבאתה אל תוך ביתך, and afterwards והסירה את שמלת שביה מעליה — and it is their way to adorn themselves in war in fine garments."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:11.322469325Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}